                           ACCEPTABLE USE NOTICE
================================================================================

This software is provided for lawful use by individuals and entities who are
enrolled members of the Apple Developer Program and who hold valid Apple-
issued signing certificates and provisioning profiles for the applications
they sign.

By obtaining, installing, or otherwise using this software, you represent and
warrant that:

  (a) you will comply with the Apple Developer Program License Agreement, the
      Apple Developer Enterprise Program License Agreement (as applicable),
      and all other Apple terms governing your use of Apple-issued signing
      identities and device provisioning;

  (b) you will use this software only to sign applications that you own,
      that you have authored, or that you are otherwise expressly authorized
      by their rights holders to resign and distribute;

  (c) you will not use this software to circumvent any technological
      protection measure, to disable or alter any Apple verification
      mechanism, or to distribute pirated, cracked, tampered, or otherwise
      unauthorized third-party applications;

  (d) you are solely responsible for compliance with all applicable laws and
      third-party agreements in your jurisdiction, including but not limited
      to copyright, computer misuse, and export-control regulations.

This software does not provide, and does not purport to provide, any means of
bypassing Apple code-signing enforcement on iOS. Every cryptographic
operation is performed locally, with keys supplied by the user, against
inputs (certificates and profiles) that Apple itself has issued to the user.
The validity of any signature produced by this software depends solely on
the validity of those Apple-issued inputs.

